A lifted free parameter whose constraint is an unexported, empty interface from
the provider's package renders as the bare "any" in the header, so the unexported
type x.c is never named across the boundary; plumb generates it rather than
rejecting it. Mirror of constraint_empty_crosspkg, but with an unexported
constraint that solve accepts because emit collapses it to any.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
output: plumb_gen.go
-- example.com/x/x.go --
package x

type c interface{}
type Box[T any] struct{}
type Out struct{}

//plumb:build
func F[T c](b Box[T]) *Out { return &Out{} }
